{
  "format": "restoreproof.jobs.v1",
  "description": "Documents the Worker's rp::parse_jobs and Python's jsonschema must judge alike against shared/schemas/jobs.v1.json, with client-profile.v1.json for each job's client (W4.10, docs/decisions.md 2026-10-09 point 8). `base` is a valid jobs document as canonical-json-v1 (one line, no trailing newline); each case is base with its RFC 6902 patch applied, `valid` says whether the schema accepts it, and `code_refuses` marks a case the schema accepts and the Worker's reader refuses (a run_id that is a DOS device's name, ends in a dot or is `..`: no folder can carry it). For the Worker a document is valid when it reads and every job of it passes every rule. No case holds a float.",
